# Transition state for K + H2O2 (2 waters, Grotthuss relay) -> KP
# (COMPUTATIONAL.md C8 item 1). See ../rc/job.inp for the full identification
# note (confirmed by direct connectivity analysis 2026-09-09) and the
# solvation/resource corrections applied here; both files carry the same
# fixes for the same reasons, not repeated in full below.
#
# The relay this TS captures (RC -> TS bond-length evidence, all four
# centres moving at once):
#   H2O2's own proton (H135) transfers to water 2 (O134)
#   water 2's own proton (H133) transfers to water 1 (O132)
#   water 1's own proton (H131) transfers to the ketone oxygen (O130)
#   H2O2's now-deprotonated oxygen (O136) simultaneously attacks the ketone
#     carbon (C129), forming the new C-O bond
# -- a four-centre concerted Grotthuss relay, not a bare HOO- addition and
# not a hydroxide-expulsion step. See conversation record 2026-09-09 for the
# full RC/TS bond-length table.
#
# Corrections from the orca_stuff version, 2026-09-09:
# 1. ALPB(Water) -> ddCOSMO(Water): so the QM1 (r2SCAN-3c) region -- where this
#    entire four-centre relay lives -- is actually solvated, not just the
#    QM2/xtb scaffold. See ../rc/job.inp for the manual citation.
# 2. Added Recalc_Hess 10: this project's first three attempts at a
#    different TS in this same QM/XTB style (K+peroxide+BnOH_bridged_
#    UNIDENTIFIED/, before its geometry was found to be misidentified)
#    plateaued for 40+ cycles on a single initial Hessian, and a second
#    attempt seeded from the drifted geometry then had 60% of its
#    displacement gradients fail outright. Recalc_Hess 10 (ORCA 6.1 manual,
#    "4.3. Transition State Searches": recommended when "the PES near the
#    TS can be very far from ideal for a Newton-Raphson step") refreshes the
#    exact Hessian periodically rather than trusting one RFO-updated
#    approximation for the whole search. Cheap here: each displacement
#    gradient on this QM region runs ~1.5 s, so a full recompute is on the
#    order of a couple of minutes at nprocs 8.
# 3. nprocs 12 / maxcore 2200 -> nprocs 8 / maxcore 4000: homelab-benchmarked
#    (COMPUTATIONAL.md Conventions, 2026-09-09).
# 4. Added AutoFF_QM2_Method GFNFF, 2026-09-17. The default GFN-xTB QM2
#    topology builder read the non-bonded O130...C59 contact (2.48 A) as a
#    QM-QM2 bond and capped the carbonyl O with a third link atom, aborting
#    ORCA's link-atom pre-optimisation before any QM1 calculation (kept in
#    attempt1_default_topology_failed/). GFN-FF's connectivity sees only the
#    two real C-C cuts. Topology only: the QM2 level (XTB2) and its Hirshfeld
#    embedding charges are unchanged. See COMPUTATIONAL.md log 2026-09-17.
# 5. Enlarged the QM region, 2026-09-17. The 12-atom region left the carbonyl's
#    two alpha-carbons in QM2, so C129 was capped by two link H and the QM1
#    electrophile was H2C=O, not the real 1,3-dialkoxy ketone (an
#    aldehyde-like carbonyl is much more electrophilic). Added the two
#    alpha-carbons (C121, C125), their CH2 hydrogens (H122/H123, H126/H127)
#    and the two beta-ether oxygens (O65, O62) -- 20 atoms, boundary now the
#    two O-C(ester) cuts O65-C59 and O62-C56. Capping the beta-O with link H
#    models the substituent as -OH rather than -OR, a residual approximation.
#    Probe confirmed 2 link atoms and a clean setup with GFNFF.
# 6. Restarted from attempt2's cycle-32 geometry, 2026-09-18. attempt2 (this
#    input, seeded from the ALPB TS) ran 240+ cycles: it reached a stationary
#    point at cycle 32 (rms 2.5e-5 and max 1.25e-4, both inside tolerance) but
#    the full-system Hessian would not settle at one negative eigenvalue (3 at
#    cycle 32; the count flipped 1-4 across the run, with several LARGE
#    imaginary modes -- -388, -519, -1150 cm-1 -- so not scaffold noise). The
#    search then wandered downhill for ~200 cycles. This restart seeds from
#    that cycle-32 frame (kept in attempt2_qm20_fullhess_stalled/, frame 32 of
#    job_trj.xyz) and adds TS_Mode {B 135 128} (the forming O136-C129 bond) and
#    TS_Active_Atoms for the relay centres, per ORCA 6.0 manual 6.3.11. The
#    converged ALPB TS is still
#    preserved at alpb_uncorrected/job_converged_alpb.xyz.
# 7. attempt3 (this input seeded from attempt2 c32, plus TS_Mode/TS_Active_
#    Atoms) also stalled, 2026-09-18: gradients converged by c11-12 but the
#    Hessian's negative-eigenvalue count flipped 1-5 and the step criteria
#    never held, so it wandered 250+ cycles. Kept in
#    attempt3_qm20_tsmode_stalled/. attempt4 seeds from attempt3 c20
#    (gradients converged, neg_eig=1) and changes the Hessian strategy:
#    Hybrid_Hess over the relay atoms (manual 6.3.11.2, for a delocalized
#    concerted mode), HESS_Modification EV_Reverse (manual 7.26, for the
#    >1-negative case), and the non-QM host frozen so its soft modes cannot
#    drive the search.
#
# Also added %output jsonpropfile true end (2026-09-17): orca_io/OPI reads the
# property JSON, which ORCA writes only when this keyword is present.
#
# The QM region otherwise follows the version that produced a QMRegion.xyz
# cleanly. Geometry (job.xyz) is the attempt3 c20 frame (correction 7), which
# sits near the ddCOSMO-level stationary region. alpb_uncorrected/
# also holds an abandoned SMD-solvation attempt (sp_abandoned_smd_attempt/)
# from before this correction; plain CPCM/SMD are both rejected outright by
# ORCA for QM/XTB (see ../rc/job.inp) -- ddCOSMO was chosen because the
# manual is explicit it gets the same C-PCM/B-style propagation to QM1.

! QM/XTB r2SCAN-3c ddCOSMO(Water) OptTS Freq TightSCF

%QMMM
QMATOMS
	{61 64 120 121 122 124 125 126 128 129 130 131 132 133 134 135 136 137 138 139}
END
Charge_total 0
Mult_total 1
AutoFF_QM2_Method GFNFF
END

%geom
Calc_Hess true
Recalc_Hess 10
# The TS mode is a delocalized four-centre relay, so per ORCA 6.0 manual
# 6.3.11.2 compute the exact numerical second derivatives only for the relay
# atoms; the rest (including the floppy 120-atom host) gets a model Hessian.
Hybrid_Hess {128 129 130 131 132 133 134 135 136 137 138 139} end
# The default Shift_Diag did not stabilise the P-RFO step with several negative
# eigenvalues; reverse the Hessian diagonal instead (manual 7.26).
HESS_Modification EV_Reverse
# Follow the forming O136-C129 bond (0-based 135-128).
TS_Mode {B 135 128} end
# Ensure the relay centres' bonds are in the internal-coordinate set
# (manual 6.3.11.1: a breaking/forming bond can be missed if its distance is
# slightly too large, "leading to slow or even no convergence").
TS_Active_Atoms {128 129 130 131 132 133 134 135 136} end
TS_Active_Atoms_Factor 1.5
# Freeze the non-QM host (0-based 0-60, 62-63, 65-119, 123, 127) so the
# macrocycle's soft modes cannot drive the search; only the QM region and its
# link shell move.
ReduceRedInts true
Constraints
  { C 0:60 C}
  { C 62 C}
  { C 63 C}
  { C 65:119 C}
  { C 123 C}
  { C 127 C}
end
END

%output jsonpropfile true end

%maxcore 4000

%pal
   nprocs 8
end

* xyzfile 0 1 job.xyz
